{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Elohim, in home</b> — after the manner of: 'for a house will be made for you by YHWH,' and 'he made them houses,' 'a man and his household,' 'a lamb for the house.' The meaning: for he sets the solitary as many and settles them." "And the word <b>with prosperity</b> is connected with <b>prisoners</b>, as if he said: bound with chains." "And the meaning of <b>prosperity</b> — the chain whose meaning [is so], like: 'she sends her hands to the spindle.'" "And the meaning of <b>the rebellious</b> — those who do violence to orphans." "And the word <b>parched</b> — like: 'he parched thirsty,' like 'and satisfy in parchedness your soul.' Dried up, and this is the opposite of 'settles the solitary in a home': formerly in settlement, now parched a place of thirst."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 68, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:04.736130245Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}